body.text:
Glory be to God for freckled things —
  For girls who know the weight of every seal and every cow;
    For calves pulled out at twelve; for hay; for strength in every limb;
For clipboards, and the six true facts a hermit brings;
  For Ropers, and a red truck’s dust, and fallow, and the plough;
    For Glory Bes on fourth and one, said quick, not like a hymn;
All things counter, original, spare, strange;
  Whatever is fickle, freckled (who knows how?)
    With swift, slow; sweet, sour; adazzle, dim;
He fathers-forth whose beauty is past change:
                        Praise him.
